Savory sweet and bold the smells envelop  you as you walk into the small kitchen  of Shea Shamus this Cuttery breakfast  Feast is served no matter the hour it  features a Bedouin bread made of flour  and water called reg gag and flavorful  stew called marguga  shamsal kasabi's restaurant in sukhwakif  is also a landmark she is the first  woman to own a Eatery in Qatar and the  first to open a business in the soup  hospitality and generosity are pillars  of the Qatari Traditions women play a  role at home when we open our doors and  welcome our neighbors and visit us with  traditional food here I will be a true  representative of the Qatari women  more than 20 years ago kasabi began  pickling lemons in her backyard and  selling them via Word of Mouth then she  opened a spy shop and eventually this  restaurant in 2014. along the way her  entrepreneurial Ambitions clashed with  her family's ideas about A Woman's Place  in the past as a conservative Society it  was difficult for women to socialize  with men I was the first to bend the  rule with some objections from my family  How could a woman work among men  kasabi's customers include the Cuttery  ruling family Foodies and footballer  David Beckham her home style cooking in  an Arab coffee shop environment is a  link to qatar's Roots  my main goal is to ensure that our  Cuisine lives on for future Generations  it's part of preserving our cultural  Traditions not only for qataris but for  visitors to our country especially since  Qatar is hosting the World Cup  last summer kasabi launched an online  store now with these jars of spices and  mixes she can share a taste of Qatar  with the world
 

